commit 43b34bebd2cb644836188fbff8c254fec0e18cf9
Author: tabnul <tabnuland@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 14:22:42 2026 +0100

    sotc: partial async readbacks, recopy after GPU writes; 240 Hz vblank
    
    Readbacks:
    - An async readback that a write dirtied while it was in flight now
      applies the clean parts of its copy. A retry only runs when the bytes
      the guest asked for changed (SOTC_RB_PARTIAL=0 restores the old path).
    - A GPU write into an in-flight readback window is copied again after
      the back op that wrote it (RecopyReadbacks), so it doesn't end up as a
      full re-read.
    - DropGpuModified requests are queued and applied on the GPU side.
    - Diagnostics: the SOTC FPS line splits the guest's readback wait into
      begin/gpu/finish ms/s, plus guest submit sequence numbers for the
      readback logs.
    
    Vblank: the launcher and sotc.py now set BB_VBLANK_HZ=240 (was 120), so a
    finished frame is shown within ~4 ms. Same average FPS on the pan30
    replay, frames over 33 ms 17 -> 8. The flip interval and SOTC_FPS_LIMIT
    already scale with the rate. @deadinside28's Bloodborne port runs its
    uncapped presets at 480-1000 Hz for the same reason.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

